    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d473">

                <pb facs="0567" n="557" sameAs="frus:frus1944v02/pg557"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.796/10–1144: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-10-11T20:00:00+01:00">October 11, 1944—8
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 9:34 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>8585. Masefield says nothing of “world shaking” consequence will develop in the
                    debate on civil aviation in the House of Lords tomorrow; that Lord Beaverbrook
                    will largely give an account of what he has done and turn over to Lord
                    Swinton.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
